      <h2>Dossier 2.0 · New October 2026: What the Federal Records Show</h2>

      <h3>Grant 03D02024</h3>

      <p>
        The USAspending.gov award record for 03D02024 names the recipient as
        "CITY OF WAYNESBORO". It shows $2,000,000 obligated and $1,292,834.94 in
        outlays. The period runs from September 1, 2023 to June 30, 2026. The
        record was last modified on April 6, 2026. It does not show whether the
        period was extended.
      </p>

      <p>
        The stated purpose is "TO UPSIZE 5,550 LINEAR FEET OF THE EXISTING
        15-INCH MAIN TO 18-INCH SEWER LINE MAIN FROM 6TH STREET CEMETERY TO 4TH
        STREET". The record does not name the development.
      </p>

      <h3>The 2026 federal grant of $1 million</h3>

      <p>
        The City's own August 17, 2026 contract with its regional commission
        names the program as the EPA's Community Grants program for fiscal year
        2026, the recipient as the City of Waynesboro, and the purpose as
        "Sanitary Sewer Improvements". In that contract's schedule every
        completion date reads "TBD" and every start date is blank. A U.S.
        Senator's release of February 19, 2026 quotes the mayor: "this
        $1,000,000 federal appropriation to advance our sanitary sewer
        improvement initiative." True Citizen reported the grant on February 24,
        2026.
      </p>

      <p>
        None of these records names the development or the developer. They name
        the City as recipient. This page does not connect either grant to St.
        George Crossing.
      </p>

      <div class="document-list">
        <a
          class="document-row"
